1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,433
In 2 + 3 and 2 · 3, the 2 has a different name.

2
00:00:06,433 --> 00:00:08,633
Things you add are terms.

3
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:12,167
Things you multiply are factors.

4
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:14,200
Here are two terms…

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:19,000
Look inside: each one has a factor of a.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,800
A factor shared by every term can step outside…

7
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,000
…a(x + 2y).

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,500
Multiply back to check: ax + 2ay. Same thing.

9
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:35,900
Pulling out a shared factor is called factoring.

10
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:42,067
It's the first step of everything that comes next.
